CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ 5 \+ 2 == 7: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG: must fail: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^found no match for symbol 'make_range'$
--
N5008 [temp.deduct]/[expr.type]: resolving a function template whose trailing
return type contains a decltype naming a parameter (`-> ranget<decltype(c.begin())>`)
must be independent of previous resolutions of the same template.  CBMC put a
synthetic parameter symbol into scope to resolve the decltype and never removed
it, so speculatively matching the one-parameter container overload of
`make_range` against a two-argument iterator call left a stale symbol of the
wrong type; the correct resolution of `make_range(container)` then evaluated
`decltype(c.begin())` against the stale type and failed ("found no match for
make_range").  Fixed in cpp_typecheck_resolvet::guess_function_template_args by
refreshing the synthetic symbol's type on each resolution.  Reduced (cvise,
real headers) from src/util/structured_data.cpp.  assertion.2 provides
non-vacuity.
